From c09d19cb6c25e5462f34b66fe8c418c49a4afb5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steve Shreeve <steve.shreeve@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:09:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] std: a Map's and Set's probes and iterators index with no
 bounds test

Each probe loop's test bounds its index by both Lists of the table, the
tags and the entry indexes, which are always the same length, so the
proof pass proves every read and write of a slot; `place` probes
itself rather than handing a slot back through `free_slot`. A small
Map's or Set's scan bounds its index by the entries as well as the
hashes, and the iterators walk a slice of the entries under a guard
of both bounds. Only an entry's index read from a slot keeps its
test. The count of entries grows by a wrapping add, as it never
passes the entries' length. std.text's Interner probes its table the
same way. test/cli/std_proofs.sh checks every index in them is proven.
